    { l: 'h6', q: 'What is the title of the national anthem?', o: ['Ons Heemecht', 'De Wilhelmus', 'Renert', 'Mir wëlle bleiwe wat mir sinn'], e: '"Ons Heemecht" (Our Homeland). De Wilhelmus is the anthem of the grand ducal family.' },
    { l: 'h6', q: 'What does the national motto "Mir wëlle bleiwe wat mir sinn" mean?', o: ['We want to remain what we are', 'Unity is strength', 'God protect the Grand Duke', 'Freedom and homeland'], e: 'The motto expresses the will to preserve Luxembourg\'s independence and identity.' },
    { l: 'h6', q: 'When is the National Day celebrated?', o: ['23 June', '9 May', '10 September', '14 July'], e: 'On 23 June, the official celebration of the Grand Duke\'s birthday, fixed since 1961/62 regardless of the actual date.' },
    { l: 'h6', q: 'What animal appears on the Luxembourg coat of arms?', o: ['A red lion', 'A golden eagle', 'A black bear', 'A white horse'], e: 'A red lion (Roude Léiw), crowned in gold, on a background of blue and white stripes.' },
    { l: 'h6', q: 'Which Luxembourg tradition is on UNESCO\'s intangible heritage list (2010)?', o: ['The hopping procession of Echternach', 'The Schueberfouer', 'The Buergbrennen', 'The Éimaischen'], e: 'The Sprangprëssioun of Echternach takes place on Whit Tuesday.' },
    { l: 'h6', q: 'Who wrote the national epic "Renert" (1872)?', o: ['Michel Rodange', 'Michel Lentz', 'Jean-Antoine Zinnen', 'Victor Hugo'], e: 'Michel Rodange\'s "Renert" (the fox) is a classic of Luxembourgish literature.' },
    { l: 'h6', q: 'Who is the patron saint of the city and country, celebrated during the Octave?', o: ['Our Lady Consoler of the Afflicted', 'Saint Willibrord', 'Saint Nicholas', 'Saint George'], e: 'The Octave pilgrimage honours Our Lady Consoler of the Afflicted. Saint Willibrord is linked to Echternach.' },
    { l: 'h6', q: 'What happens on the evening of 22 June?', o: ['Torchlight procession and fireworks in the capital', 'The Schueberfouer opens', 'Elections are held', 'The Octave begins'], e: 'The eve of the National Day is celebrated with a torchlight procession and fireworks. The 23rd has a military parade and the Te Deum.' },
    { tf: true, l: 'h6', q: 'The old town and fortifications of Luxembourg City are a UNESCO World Heritage site.', a: true, e: 'True. They were listed in 1994.' }
